WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:05.069
Emperor Palpatine will return in Star Wars
Episode IX: The Rise of Skywalker, and he

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:09.760
won't be stopping by for a cameo despite what
actor Ian McDiarmid might say:

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:16.059
"I have to be honest with you: I was in the
area, so I thought the least I could do is

00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:17.670
to pop in for a laugh."

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:19.280
All joking aside…

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:24.710
Speaking with IGN at Disney's D23 Expo, stars
Daisy Ridley, John Boyega, and Kelly Marie

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:29.350
Tran offered some insight into the importance
of the dastardly figure who was famously thought

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:34.481
to have perished at the conclusion of 1983's
Star Wars Episode VI: Return of the Jedi to

00:00:34.481 --> 00:00:35.630
the flick's story.

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:39.910
Fans were shocked when Palpatine's distinctive
laugh was heard at the end of the first teaser

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:44.240
trailer for Rise of Skywalker, and it was
made explicit that this was no misdirection

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:47.750
when the movie's first poster was revealed
at D23.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:55.250
"No one's ever really gone…"

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:56.760
(laughs)

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:01.289
The poster features the Emperor's visage floating
above Ridley's Rey and Adam Driver's Kylo

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:03.860
Ren as they face off in a lightsaber duel.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:08.170
In the same way that his likeness looms over
the poster's imagery, Boyega astutely pointed

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:12.610
out that Palpatine's machinations loom large
over the entire Star Wars series.

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:13.659
He explained:

00:01:13.659 --> 00:01:17.670
"I think the Emperor and his doctrine has
trickled down to so many of the characters

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:21.570
in the Star Wars universe, and that the Dark
Side [of the Force] is what it is because

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:23.460
of a lot of his actions and plans.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:27.820
And so, to have him come back, he's like the
greatest foe, and greatest enemy…

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:30.530
I mean, we might as well take him down properly."

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:34.960
Ridley similarly called attention to the importance
of the character to the overall narrative

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:39.260
of the Skywalker Saga, and assured fans that
his reappearance after seemingly having met

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:43.490
his end at the hands of the redeemed Anakin
Skywalker was not a plot development that

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:45.390
was taken lightly by the filmmakers.

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:46.530
Ridley said:

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:49.189
"He's the biggest baddie in Star Wars history…

00:01:49.189 --> 00:01:52.490
now that we've done the story, I'm like, it
couldn't have happened any other way.

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:53.950
Like, it had to be that.

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:57.100
But he's very, you know, instrumental to the
plot of the film.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:00.000
It's not just like he appears again; it's
all explained."

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.229
Asked about her take on the way director J.J.
Abrams and company brought the epic nine-film

00:02:04.229 --> 00:02:06.580
saga to its conclusion, Ridley said:

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:07.689
"I think it's awesome.

00:02:07.689 --> 00:02:11.650
When we were doing it, I kept going, 'Oh my
god, this is so cool.'

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:15.840
And that's nice to be in a film where you're
actually saying, 'Oh my god, this is so cool.'"

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:20.469
For her part, it seemed to be all Tran could
do to keep from spoiling the entire movie.

00:02:20.469 --> 00:02:21.469
She said:

00:02:21.469 --> 00:02:25.519
"I mean, I think that there are so many themes
in the Star Wars films… my favorite being

00:02:25.519 --> 00:02:29.999
redemption, and this idea of, like, whatever
comes at you, you can… well, I'm not gonna

00:02:29.999 --> 00:02:33.730
give you, I'm not gonna tell you what happens,
but… the theme of redemption."

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:38.650
Pressed on exactly what her comments meant
in regards to Palpatine, Tran grinned mischievously

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:40.919
and said, quote, "Look, I don't know."

00:02:40.919 --> 00:02:45.090
Of course, the stars were also grilled over
Rey's seeming transformation in the new footage

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:48.480
from Rise of Skywalker which was screened
at D23.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:53.409
Said footage saw her cloaked and hooded, wielding
a distinctive, Darth Maul-esque red, double-bladed

00:02:53.409 --> 00:02:57.469
lightsaber suggesting that before it's all
said and done, the character could be taking

00:02:57.469 --> 00:03:01.909
a walk on the Dark Side, a development which
could be strongly tied to Palpatine's return.

00:03:01.909 --> 00:03:06.599
Their responses were right in line with their
previous remarks: Boyega's was cheeky, Tran's

00:03:06.599 --> 00:03:10.280
was carefully worded, and Ridley's was downright
evasive.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:12.620
After the apparent "Dark Rey" reveal, Boyega
quipped:

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:14.939
"For me, it's just a mere costume change.

00:03:14.939 --> 00:03:16.590
I mean, the girl wanted dark.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:19.069
I wear black sometimes, doesn't mean I'm bad.

00:03:19.069 --> 00:03:20.069
The red?

00:03:20.069 --> 00:03:21.069
It's a glow stick thing."

00:03:21.069 --> 00:03:22.069
He also added,

00:03:22.069 --> 00:03:24.409
"I don't think the fans should really get
into all of that.

00:03:24.409 --> 00:03:28.709
What you need to look at is how C-3PO got
his golden arm back… that's the question

00:03:28.709 --> 00:03:29.709
for me."

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:34.199
Tran, when asked about the reveal, offered
up this cornucopia of vagueness, saying:

00:03:34.199 --> 00:03:38.040
"I think the most important thing to take
from that whole snippet is just that the ending

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:42.419
of this film is going to be really… really
groundbreaking, in a good way.

00:03:42.419 --> 00:03:46.169
I think there are a lot of little pieces from
the older films, and everyone's together in

00:03:46.169 --> 00:03:49.469
this one, and it's a really big… we're gonna
go out with a bang."

00:03:49.469 --> 00:03:54.889
Ridley, while no more inclined toward specificity,
did tease that Rise of Skywalker will revisit

00:03:54.889 --> 00:03:58.879
the themes of the previous films in putting
a bow on the Skywalker Saga.

00:03:58.879 --> 00:03:59.879
She revealed:

00:03:59.879 --> 00:04:03.499
"I think [the movie] should, hopefully, show
people that we did a big old journey, and

00:04:03.499 --> 00:04:04.799
we explored some things.

00:04:04.799 --> 00:04:06.839
So, just you wait 'til the film [comes out]."

00:04:06.839 --> 00:04:09.290
Thank you for stating the obvious.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:12.930
To find out for sure how Rey and friends wrap
up their story, we'll just have to wait until

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:17.310
Star Wars Episode IX: The Rise of Skywalker
hits theaters on December 20.

